    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">

  <header>
    <h1>Climate Change 2023: Key Findings</h1>
    <p>A visual summary of the most critical findings from the IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report, highlighting observed changes, future projections, and urgent pathways for climate action.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="metrics-grid">
    <div class="metric-card critical">
      <div class="metric-value">3.3–3.6B</div>
      <div class="metric-label">People exposed to severe climate hazards</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-card solution">
      <div class="metric-value">43%</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Required GHG reduction by 2030 (vs 2019)</div>
    </div>

    <div class="sub-metrics">
        <div class="metric-card" style="border-top-color: var(--accent-red);">
          <div class="metric-value" style="color: var(--accent-red);">+1.1°C</div>
          <div class="metric-label">Global surface temp increase (vs 1850–1900)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card" style="border-top-color: var(--accent-vermilion);">
          <div class="metric-value" style="color: var(--accent-vermilion);">410 ppm</div>
          <div class="metric-label">CO₂ concentration (highest in 2M years)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card" style="border-top-color: var(--accent-amber);">
          <div class="metric-value" style="color: var(--accent-amber);">~59 Gt</div>
          <div class="metric-label">Global GHG emissions (2019)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card" style="border-top-color: var(--accent-teal);">
          <div class="metric-value" style="color: var(--accent-teal);">~500 Gt</div>
          <div class="metric-label">Remaining carbon budget for 1.5°C</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card" style="border-top-color: var(--accent-blue);">
          <div class="metric-value" style="color: var(--accent-blue);">~0.20 m</div>
          <div class="metric-label">Sea level rise (1901–2018)</div>
        </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-grid">
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Observed Changes & Current State</h2>
      <p>Human-caused climate change is unequivocally affecting every region on Earth, with widespread and intensifying consequences.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Extreme Weather:</strong> Increases in frequency and intensity of heatwaves, heavy precipitation, droughts, and tropical cyclones.</li>
        <li><strong>Emissions Sources:</strong> Fossil fuel combustion and land-use change dominate the ~59 GtCO₂e annual emissions.</li>
        <li><strong>Irreversible Shifts:</strong> Ocean warming, acidification, and sea-level rise are already locked in for centuries.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>Risks & Cascading Impacts</h2>
      <p>Climate hazards increasingly interact with non-climatic stressors—poverty, inequality, ecosystem degradation—to produce compounding risks.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Food & Water:</strong> Crop yield growth rates have slowed; over half the global population experiences severe water scarcity.</li>
        <li><strong>Biodiversity Loss:</strong> Accelerates beyond 1.5°C; up to 14% of terrestrial species face very high extinction risk at 1.5°C.</li>
        <li><strong>Health:</strong> Expanding ranges of vector-borne diseases and rising heat-related mortality.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section projections">
      <h2>Future Projections Under Different Scenarios (by 2100)</h2>
      <p>The severity of future climate outcomes depends entirely on the trajectory of global emissions across Shared Socioeconomic Pathways (SSPs).</p>
      <div class="scenario-strip">
        <div class="scenario ssp1-19">
          <h3>SSP1-1.9</h3>
          <div class="temp">~1.4°C</div>
          <div class="desc">Very low emissions<br>Sustainability focus</div>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario ssp1-26">
          <h3>SSP1-2.6</h3>
          <div class="temp">~1.8°C</div>
          <div class="desc">Low emissions<br>Rapid decline</div>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario ssp2-45">
          <h3>SSP2-4.5</h3>
          <div class="temp">~2.7°C</div>
          <div class="desc">Intermediate emissions<br>Current trends</div>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario ssp3-70">
          <h3>SSP3-7.0</h3>
          <div class="temp">~3.6°C</div>
          <div class="desc">High emissions<br>Regional rivalry</div>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario ssp5-85">
          <h3>SSP5-8.5</h3>
          <div class="temp">~4.4°C</div>
          <div class="desc">Very high emissions<br>Fossil-fuel intensive</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section mitigation">
      <h2>Mitigation and Adaptation Pathways</h2>
      <div>
        <p style="font-size: 40px; color: var(--text-main);">To limit warming to <strong>1.5°C</strong>, global GHG emissions must reach <strong>net zero CO₂ by ~2050</strong>. For 2°C, net zero by ~2070 is required.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Energy:</strong> Rapid decarbonization, massive expansion of renewables, and electrification of transport.</li>
          <li><strong>Demand:</strong> Efficiency improvements and behavioral shifts across all sectors.</li>
          <li><strong>Sinks:</strong> Protection and restoration of natural carbon sinks, including forests and oceans.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="narrowing-window">
      <h2>The Narrowing Window for Action</h2>
      <p>The choices made in this decade will determine whether warming can be held to 1.5°C or 2°C. Delayed action increases costs, locks in high-carbon infrastructure, and severely limits the feasibility of keeping warming within safe limits. Immediate, deep, and sustained emissions reductions are essential to secure a liveable and sustainable future for all.</p>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
